<HelpTab>
    <HelpSection Title="Who has set up their phone">
        <FluentText>
            <strong>Staff Set-up</strong>, under Management › People, lists everyone at the location you're signed in
            to. Each person shows three ticks or crosses:
        </FluentText>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>App</strong>: they've opened Lanyard from their Home Screen on at least one phone or tablet.</li>
            <li><strong>Notifications</strong>: notifications are on for at least one of their devices.</li>
            <li><strong>Face ID</strong>: they've set up Face ID or fingerprint sign-in. This one is optional.</li>
        </ul>
        <FluentText>
            Someone counts as ready once they have both the app and notifications. The top of the page shows how many are
            ready, and <strong>Only show who isn't ready</strong> hides everyone else. Select a name to open their profile.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Getting people set up">
        <FluentText>
            Select <strong>Copy set-up link</strong> and send it to anyone who isn't ready, or turn it into a QR code to
            put on screen. It opens Get Started, which takes each person through installing the app and turning on
            notifications on their own phone.
        </FluentText>
        <HelpNote>
            The list only knows about a phone once its owner has opened the app on it while signed in. Ask anyone
            who says they've done it but still shows a cross to open the app once.
        </HelpNote>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
